! GAMESS/VB2000 Test 35
!
! This is a more standard (compared with the simple run on H2 in
! exam-vb29) test of using GVB for the initial guess. It involves
! a preliminary run to get a $VEC block for GUESS=MOREAD in GUESS
! as documented below.
!
! The GVB energy is -40.2416023819 
!
! The VB(8) energy is -40.2435441021
!
! This function is essentially the GVB function with the 
! orthogonality restriction between pairs removed. You can
! use VB2000 to confirm the GVB energy by replacing VB(8)
! on the #! line with VB(2).VB(2).VB(2).VB(2), and altering
! GRPDIM to 1,2,2,2,2. Note that the GRPDIM directive is 
! always required for GVB initial guess runs.
!
! The block below is for the final run.
 $CONTRL SCFTYP=GVB RUNTYP=ENERGY COORD=UNIQUE
 ICHARG=0 MULT=1 VBTYP=VB2000 $END
 $SCF NCO=1 NSETO=0 NPAIR=4 $END
 $SYSTEM TIMLIM=2 MEMORY=1000000 $END
 $BASIS  GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 $END
 $GUESS  GUESS=MOREAD NORB=9 NORDER=1 
   IORDER(2)=2,8,3,7,4,6,5,9 $END
!
! This block below is for the initial run.
! $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=ENERGY COORD=UNIQUE
! LOCAL=BOYS ICHARG=0 MULT=1 $END
! $SCF VVOS=.T. $END
! $SYSTEM TIMLIM=2 MEMORY=1000000 $END
! $BASIS  GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 $END
! $GUESS  GUESS=HUCKEL $END
! VVOS=.T. in $SCF creates a set of valence virtual orbitals that
! are more compact than the normal virtuals. LOCAL=BOYS creates
! localised MOs, for the occupied MOs and the VVOs.
! After running this data you have to carefully inspect the LMOs.
! Using MacMolPlt is a good way. You have to pair the bonding and
! antibonding LMOs for GUESS=MOREAD. Then add exam-vb36.dat to the
! end of the input file and remove the first two $VEC groups, 
! leaving only the one for the LMOs.
!
 $DATA  
Methane 6-31G                                                                  
C1       0
C           6.0      0.0000000000      0.0000000000      0.0000000000
H1          1.0      0.6300000000     -0.6300000000     -0.6300000000
H2          1.0      0.6300000000      0.6300000000      0.6300000000
H3          1.0     -0.6300000000      0.6300000000     -0.6300000000
H4          1.0     -0.6300000000     -0.6300000000      0.6300000000
 $END      
 $VB2000
#! VB(8)/6-31G PRINTALL

Methane 6-31G

0 1

 $GRPDIM
 1,8

 $ECONV
 8

 $MACROITER
 20

 $DENSCUBE
 DENS GMSD HPRT
 H2 CCT
 81

 $END      
BOYS LOCALIZED ORBITALS
 $VEC
 1  1 9.97062044E-01 2.38049590E-02 5.68544573E-09-3.73763437E-10-2.89978405E-09
 1  2-1.82974693E-02-3.90570546E-09 2.91719449E-10 1.97478267E-09-7.56236552E-04
 1  3 2.95386832E-03-7.56233875E-04 2.95386532E-03-7.56231583E-04 2.95386276E-03
 1  4-7.56229620E-04 2.95386045E-03
